Using `fields.data()` avoids the `operator[]` wrapper and lets the compiler emit a single pointer add after the bounds check, with the ternary keeping the null path branch-free in the common case.

```cpp
Field* Mesg::GetFieldByIndex(const FIT_UINT16 index)
{
    return (index < fields.size()) ? (fields.data() + index) : FIT_NULL;
}
```